Hey guys, it looks like I'll be writing the "Did you know ..." feature
for the webzine, at least for the first issue.  The problem is, the
only Roguelike I play is Nethack, so I don't really know anything
about the others.  Anyone have any good "Did you knows" for other
Roguelikes.  They're basically short pieces of information which are
to be compiled into a list and provide useful information you might
not know about your favorite Roguelikes.  For example, here are some
from Nethack ...

* Did you know that in addition to leaving a corpse behind, a quantum
mechanic can leave a box which has a 50/50 chance of containing either
a corpse of a cat formerly owned by Schroedinger or a live cat?
* Did you know that there is a small chance that when a shrieker
shrieks, it summons a purple worm?  (BTW - what is this an homage to?)
* Did you know that reading a scroll of enchant weapon while wielding
a worm tooth will turn it into a chrysknife, but it reverts when you
drop it?  (This is from Dune)
* Did you know that the code for a Beholder style enemy ala the
Floating Eye exists, but is commented out?
* Did you know that in much earlier versions of Nethack, wizards
started off with an athame instead of a quarterstaff?

... etc ...

Also, if you wish to keep the contributions secret until the webzine
is published (so that the webzine contains new information, not just
stuff that everyone has already read on here), you can e-mail them to
me.  Credit will be given to all contributors.

Thanks!

